definitions.documentation:
# SQLite Statement List / statements Value

Exact structural field contract extracted from SQLite Statement List. Optional presence belongs to the containing node socket; null is accepted only when this schema explicitly allows it. Required object fields and list element schemas are checked at runtime. Extension values use the explicit recursive ONFJsonValue vocabulary. This type has pure JSON Encode/Decode codecs.

## Audited socket contract (21 October 2026)

Inputs:
No data sockets.

Outputs:
No data sockets.

Configuration:
No asset-specific configuration.

Known provider records and list elements have structural schemas. Explicit dynamic payloads, selected query results and provider extensions retain the recursive JSON Value vocabulary; they do not imply a known provider entity. Null is distinct from omission. Runtime validates the exact selected immutable type version; reading newer documentation never repins existing graphs. This audit used synthetic fixtures/local mocks and does not establish live provider authorization or delivery.

Authoritative JSON Schema:

```json
{
  "type": "array",
  "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "sql": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1,
        "maxLength": 100000
      },
      "params": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": [
            "string",
            "number",
            "null"
          ]
        },
        "maxItems": 1000
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "sql"
    ],
    "additionalProperties": false
  },
  "maxItems": 100
}
```

Library registry key: `core.sqlite.transaction.contract.field.statements`.

